[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3954950223","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116735#issuecomment-3954950223","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116735","id":3954950223,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ru8BP","user":{"login":"LemmaEOF","id":6722691,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjI2OTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6722691?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF","html_url":"https://github.com/LemmaEOF","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T21:55:39Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T21:55:39Z","body":"I'm not sure this is very useful without #107226's `AudioServer.get_absolute_time()` method - having a way to set the specific start time absolutely, instead of relative to other audio tracks that may or may not exist, is kinda essential.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3954950223/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3954977259","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116735#issuecomment-3954977259","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116735","id":3954977259,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rvCnr","user":{"login":"BuzzLord","id":11238951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjM4OTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11238951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord","html_url":"https://github.com/BuzzLord","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T22:02:29Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T22:02:29Z","body":"> I'm not sure this is very useful without #107226's `AudioServer.get_absolute_time()` method - having a way to set the specific start time absolutely, instead of relative to other audio tracks that may or may not exist, is kinda essential.\r\n\r\nCan you give an example of a situation where you'd need absolute time? I was picturing the issue as needing a way to schedule sounds to play at specific times so they lined up with other sounds or background music or something... always relative to something else. But I'm admittedly not the target audience of this change.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3954977259/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3954990595","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116735#issuecomment-3954990595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116735","id":3954990595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rvF4D","user":{"login":"LemmaEOF","id":6722691,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjI2OTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6722691?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF","html_url":"https://github.com/LemmaEOF","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T22:05:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T22:05:23Z","body":"A specific use case of mine right now is a count-in metronome before a song begins in a rhythm game - the metronome sound effects happen *before* the main background music starts playing and are too short to be used as the base reference for a synchronized stream, so they need to have access to an absolute time in order to sync properly with the song.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3954990595/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955024999","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116735#issuecomment-3955024999","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116735","id":3955024999,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rvORn","user":{"login":"BuzzLord","id":11238951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjM4OTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11238951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord","html_url":"https://github.com/BuzzLord","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T22:11:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T22:11:43Z","body":"You can just have the song start at the delay then. Metronome sounds play at time 0.0, 1.0, 2.0, etc, then the main song starts at 5.0. All subsequent sounds can play based off that offset.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955024999/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955069221","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116735#issuecomment-3955069221","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116735","id":3955069221,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rvZEl","user":{"login":"LemmaEOF","id":6722691,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjI2OTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6722691?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF","html_url":"https://github.com/LemmaEOF","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T22:20:40Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T22:20:40Z","body":"Ehhh, I still feel like having the option for absolute time is important enough to consider - it gives more flexibility as to how you can approach things rather than just being locked into relative start times. This doesn't feel like it properly covers the use cases as well as 107226, given it also doesn't have support for dynamically adding streams.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955069221/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3957273872","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116735#issuecomment-3957273872","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116735","id":3957273872,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7r3zUQ","user":{"login":"PizzaLovers007","id":10912951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTEyOTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10912951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007","html_url":"https://github.com/PizzaLovers007","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T07:07:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T07:07:16Z","body":"Thanks for investigating! Being able to dynamically add streams would definitely be necessary if we were to move forward with this approach. Additionally, a large portion of the use cases would likely reuse the same stream multiple times (hitsounds/metronome), so having each scheduled hit require its own stream is a bit clunky. I think the actual overlapping feature set between AudioStreamSynchronized and scheduled sounds is minimal, so there would need to be some significant rework to make it easier to use. If we were to consider the best practices here of \"to each problem, its own solution\", maybe introducing another AudioStream type for this specific problem would be better suited? I do know we were trying to avoid that from the meeting discussion though 😅","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3957273872/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3957500693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116735#issuecomment-3957500693","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116735","id":3957500693,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7r4qsV","user":{"login":"BuzzLord","id":11238951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjM4OTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11238951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord","html_url":"https://github.com/BuzzLord","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T08:03:21Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T08:03:21Z","body":"After playing around with this change, reading about how Unity does it (which your PR duplicates very closely), and thinking of some counter examples, I'm convinced that your PR is the way to go.\r\n\r\nThis PR _could_ be changed to allow for dynamically adding streams, or rescheduling sounds within the stream playback, but I think the biggest drawback is just having all the sync'd audio go through the same stream playback, and thus the same audio bus, with the same mixing. You couldn't do something like Hi-Fi Rush, where there are lots of audio sources in the world, and you want to optionally schedule them to play on the beat.\r\n\r\nI also think that using the absolute time the way you implemented it is the best way to do it. This PR does nearly the same thing, but the time is the local playback time, rather than the global playback time. No need to use a reference audio playback to be relative to.\r\n\r\nI don't know if this PR is worth keeping. It does allow for shifting the start time of sync'd sounds, which may be a useful feature. I'll leave it as draft for now, but I'm going to advocate for your PR to be merged.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3957500693/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]